       'Scientia Prima, Ep. 2: The Heart Is the Whole Conversation',
       'George Leith and Dr. Fernando Rivas Oliveras on why cardiac screening decides who can be treated with ibogaine, and what the clinic watches for after.',
       '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scientia Prima is the podcast of Transcend Ibogaine Clinic in Cancún. In episode two, host George Leith sits down with Dr. Fernando Rivas Oliveras, the clinic’s medical director, to talk about the organ that decides whether an ibogaine treatment can go ahead at all: the heart."}]},{"type":"youtube","attrs":{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W_3MTH8TQIE"}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What the episode covers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why every prospective patient is screened before acceptance, and why the medical director personally approves or declines each one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What the clinic’s team, drawn from emergency medicine, critical care, cardiology and psychiatry, watches for during 24/7 monitoring."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why trust between a patient and the people around them matters as much as the protocol."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Where to listen"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Episodes 1 and 2 are on Transcend Clinic’s YouTube channel. Scientia Prima is listed in the Eye Today directory under Podcasts."}]},{"type":"pullQuote","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Disclosure: Scientia Prima is produced by Transcend Ibogaine Clinic, which is owned by the publisher of Eye Today. Eye Today’s editorial policy applies."}]}]}'::jsonb,
       '<p>Scientia Prima is the podcast of Transcend Ibogaine Clinic in Cancún. In episode two, host George Leith sits down with Dr. Fernando Rivas Oliveras, the clinic’s medical director, to talk about the organ that decides whether an ibogaine treatment can go ahead at all: the heart.</p><div data-youtube-video=""><iframe width="640" height="360" allowfullscreen="true" rel="1" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/W_3MTH8TQIE?rel=1" start="0"></iframe></div><h2>What the episode covers</h2><p>Why every prospective patient is screened before acceptance, and why the medical director personally approves or declines each one.</p><p>What the clinic’s team, drawn from emergency medicine, critical care, cardiology and psychiatry, watches for during 24/7 monitoring.</p><p>Why trust between a patient and the people around them matters as much as the protocol.</p><h2>Where to listen</h2><p>Episodes 1 and 2 are on Transcend Clinic’s YouTube channel. Scientia Prima is listed in the Eye Today directory under Podcasts.</p><blockquote data-type="pull-quote" class="pull-quote">Disclosure: Scientia Prima is produced by Transcend Ibogaine Clinic, which is owned by the publisher of Eye Today. Eye Today’s editorial policy applies.</blockquote>',
